# Measured by a counted run through core/scripts/hermetic-run.sh (the judge's own J3 output), twice, identical.
# 54 -> 67 with arm A9 and mutants MC1 and MTAG: A9's base drive and the four per-push mutant drives (MC1 on A9 and A3,
# MTAG on A1 and A3), each one runner start, its rc generation and its judge start.
# 67 -> 76 with arm A10 and mutant MREL: A10's base drive and MREL's two per-push drives (A10, A1), three starts each.
# 76 -> 191 with arms K1-K6 and mutants MKEY, MIDC, MLEG, MUNC, MJROW, MLOK, MLDIR and MCOL (BL-1057): the six base
# K drives and the sixteen per-push mutant drives (each on its deciding K arm and twin K1, or K4 for MKEY). The judge
# starts are --key-rows, --identity-check, --legacy-ok and --store-key calls and the K5 counted write; the runner starts
# are K5's two runner drives per world; the collector starts are K6 and MCOL's dry run and apply.
191 *
107 scripts/validate-fixture-invocations.sh
33 core/scripts/hermetic-run.sh
4 scripts/collect-counted-stores.sh
